{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>The clean.</b> For at that time all of them were fit for sacrifice, as our Sages of blessed memory mentioned; and likewise in respect of their nourishing quality — the opposite of וְנִטְמֵתֶם בָּם (Leviticus 11:43)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "Sforno reads the distinction between clean and unclean animals at Noah's time as applying both to fitness for sacrifice and to dietary quality, contrasting the latter with the defiling effect of unclean creatures stated in וְנִטְמֵתֶם בָּם."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:28:34.376020157Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}